{"type":"text","timestamp":1789792646004,"sessionID":"ses_f4810bfebffeApNO7X3dNhAmLI","part":{"id":"prt_0b7f458d3001qM0Wwc2YtdpL8H","messageID":"msg_0b7f4519a001JcTanOtA0hlnKd","sessionID":"ses_f4810bfebffeApNO7X3dNhAmLI","type":"text","text":"Fixed the ownership regression with focused changes to four Lua source files.\n\n### Changes\n- Restored token comparison in `src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua`, so stale workers receive the existing lock-mismatch error before modifying recovered jobs.\n- Restored ownership checks in `extendLock-2.lua` and `extendLocks-1.lua`, preventing stale renewals from replacing the current owner’s token or extending its lock.\n- Moved delayed-job promotion in `retryJob-11.lua` after ownership validation, preventing rejected retries from changing queue state or emitting events.\n- Preserved missing-lock errors and the administrative token-zero bypass.\n\nAdded `tests/worker_ownership.redis.test.ts` with six regression cases covering recovered-job transitions, stored data and event preservation, single and batch renewal, valid-owner completion, and administrative behavior.\n\n### Verification\nUsing Node **24.21.0**:\n- `npm run build` — passed.\n- Your exact seven-file regression command — **268 tests passed**.\n- New ownership regression suite — **6 tests passed**.\n- Formatting and `git diff --check` — passed.","time":{"start":1789792639187,"end":1789792646002},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_039530d86816c064016aae117f26fc87d18862e4b99e02b479","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
